# Optional. By default the page talks to the server that served it (same origin), so a production build needs nothing.
# For `npm run dev` (Vite on another port), copy to .env.local and set the backend's base URL (http or https; the
# WebSocket URL is derived from it). The server refuses WebSockets from other origins, so also set the server's
# PUBLIC_ORIGIN to the Vite page's origin (e.g. http://localhost:5173) while developing this way.
# Vite inlines VITE_* variables into the page at build time, so never put a secret here.
# VITE_SERVER_URL=http://localhost:8080
